hw/scr/ - Vivado batch scripts
==============================

Tcl driven headless (vivado -mode batch), so the whole FPGA flow is
scriptable and diffable - no GUI, no project files checked in. Each flow script
takes [board] [period_ns] [step_div] [rows] [cols] tclargs (defaults:
nexys_a7, 10 ns, 2, 4, 4). fmax uses [board] [lo_ns] [hi_ns] [iters]
[step_div] [rows] [cols]. geometry.tcl validates positive dimensions and <=16
PEs; nondefault shapes write to build/vivado/RxC/.

    constraints.tcl  NOT a flow: defines cgra_timing_constraints <period_ns>,
                     sourced by the others. All timing lives here (create_clock,
                     async-I/O false paths, the datapath multicycle) so one knob
                     -- the period -- drives the whole flow and the Fmax sweep.
                     The board .xdc carry only physical (pin/IO/config) data.
    timing_checks.tcl Shared numeric/STA gates: invalid numbers and empty paths
                     fail. test/test_timing.tcl exercises the script decisions
                     using synthetic Vivado answers; it does not verify a netlist.
    floorplan.tcl    NOT a flow: defines cgra_floorplan <board>, sourced when
                     FLOORPLAN=1. Pblocks the PE array into one compact box
                     over a DSP column to shorten the datapath routes.
    synth.tcl        SYNTHESIS ONLY (no place/route): post-synth checkpoint +
                     utilization/timing reports, exit non-zero on any ERROR or
                     CRITICAL WARNING. The fast RTL gate (~seconds) -- run first.
    fmax.tcl         binary-search the maximum closing clock frequency and print
                     the limiting path (what to optimise next). Appends a row to
                     build/vivado/fmax_validated_history.csv (the improvement trail). Set
                     FLOORPLAN=1 to fold in the floorplan.
    build.tcl        synth + implementation + write_bitstream. Refuses to write a
                     new bitstream unless setup AND hold timing are met.
                     Old files may remain after a failed build.
    timing.tcl       STA GATE: synth + impl + report, exit non-zero unless
                     nonempty paths have WNS >= 0 and WHS >= 0.
    program.tcl      open the hw_server, find the FPGA, download a .bit.

Invoked by hw.mk (BOARD defaults to nexys_a7 = Nexys 4 DDR):
    make -f hw.mk test-scripts       # offline Tcl control-flow regression
    make -f hw.mk synth              # synth.tcl (synthesis-only gate)
    make -f hw.mk fmax               # fmax.tcl  (max frequency + bottleneck)
    make -f hw.mk bit   [PERIOD=]    # build.tcl (timing-gated bitstream)
    make -f hw.mk sta   [PERIOD=]    # timing.tcl (STA gate)
    make -f hw.mk sta FLOORPLAN=1    # any of the above, with the floorplan
    make -f hw.mk prog               # program.tcl
    make -f hw.mk bit MESH_ROWS=2 MESH_COLS=3
    make -f hw.mk prog MESH_ROWS=2 MESH_COLS=3  # same shape selects its bitstream

Vivado is not packaged in flake.nix (proprietary). For flashing without it,
use `make -f hw.mk prog-ofl` (openFPGALoader).

Fmax is reported as 1000 / the period validated by the final implementation.
No WNS extrapolation is used. The binary search is a heuristic over placement
runs; it does not establish a global maximum. phys_opt may worsen timing, so
the final run has its own gate. Reports and a checkpoint retain that run.
The constraint period does not change the board oscillator. Actual Vivado
runs must still verify selector coverage, exceptions and unconstrained paths.
